exports[`Diagnostic Showcase DefaultsSyntax.es should render the same report every time 1`] = `
"[default-on-function-literal]
Error: A Function literal can not carry a default
   ╭─┤ DefaultsSyntax.es:9:41 │
   │
 9 │     constant shorten = (_ count: Integer = 1) -> Integer {
   │                                            ▲  
   │                                            ╰── this default
   │ 
   │ Help: Write the default on the named Function or Method this value is passed to.
   │ 
   │ Note: A Function literal is called through the Function Type it was written for, which fixes how many Arguments every call passes, so a default here could never be reached.
───╯

[default-on-protocol-requirement]
Error: A Protocol requirement can not carry a default
    ╭─┤ DefaultsSyntax.es:16:27 │
    │
 16 │        trim(at side: Integer = 1) -> Self
    │                                ▲  
    │                                ╰── this default
    │ 
    │ Help: Declare the requirement without the default, and write the default on the fulfilling Method.
    │ 
    │ Note: A requirement says which calls a conforming Type must answer; a default is part of how one of them answers, which is each Namespace's own.
────╯

[case-default-without-payload]
