exports[`Module Diagnostic Showcase Ping.es should render the same report every time: Ping.es 1`] = `
"[cyclic-constant-import]
Error: Constant 'STEP' is imported across a cycle
   ╭─┤ Ping.es:2:2 │
   │
 2 │     STEP from "./Pong.es"
   │     ──┬─  
   │       ╰─── this Constant is not readable here
   │ 
   │ Help: Move the Constant into a Module outside the cycle, or expose it as a Function.
   │ 
   │ Note 1: ./Pong.es imports this Module back, directly or through further Modules.
   │ Note 2: A Function, a Type Alias, a Choice, a Protocol and a Namespace are all hoisted, so a cycle can name any of them. A Constant is not: its value exists only once its Module's body has run, and inside a cycle which body runs first is not something the source states.
───╯

[cyclic-side-effects]
Warning: This Statement runs in an order the cycle does not state
    ╭─┤ Ping.es:11:2 │
    │
 11 │     Terminal.inspect(stepped(1)::toString())
    │     ────────────────────┬───────────────────  
    │                         ╰───────────────────── this runs when the Module body runs
    │ 
    │ Help: Break the cycle, or move the Statement into a Module outside it.
    │ 
    │ Note 1: This Module is in a cycle with ./Pong.es.
    │ Note 2: A Module body runs once, on first import. Inside a cycle there is no first — whichever Module is reached first runs first, and that is decided by the entry point rather than by any of them.
────╯

─── 1 error, 1 warning
"
`;

